  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISF Western Balkans: The Kosovo SLAPPs Pilot</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project addressed the critical issue of political and commercial interests using legal measures to shut down transparency and accountability mechanisms in Kosovo. Vested interests use Strategic Litigation Against Public Participation (SLAPPs) to place financial, legal, and psychological pressure on legitimate actors, particularly investigative journalists and civil society, to stop them holding elites to account. SLAPPs prevent public criticism and exposure of corruption and serious organised crime associated with politically and financially powerful individuals. This is particularly important in an election year as these measures have a broader chilling effect on public debate when it is most needed. The outcomes from this pilot project will generate recommendations for tackling the issue in Kosovo and can be used by across the Western Balkans as it affects the whole region.</narrative>
  </description>
